  "id": "ua-pulaski-technical-college-aas-early-childhood-education",
  "major": "Early Childhood Education",
  "notes": "Meets the competencies required for the Birth through Pre-Kindergarten Teaching Credential required by Act 187 (Arkansas Legislature, 2009 session); graduates may apply for the credential from the Division of Early Care and Education of the Department of Human Services. Graduates may serve as lead teacher in a non-public school classroom or Head Start classroom (while continuing toward a bachelor's degree) and as a paraprofessional in a public school pre-kindergarten classroom; the program does NOT qualify a graduate to be the lead teacher in a public school pre-kindergarten classroom. Students must obtain cleared criminal, FBI, and child maltreatment registry checks and a UA-PTC Education ID badge prior to enrollment in ECD and ECTC courses. Students must earn a C or better in all courses taken to satisfy this AAS; minimum 2.00 cumulative GPA required for graduation. Special program fees apply. Additional prerequisite courses may be required if minimum placement test scores are not met. Work with an Education advisor for recommended full-time or part-time sequencing and degree-emphasis electives.\n\nCORRECTION 2026-10-01: ECED 10093 (Foundations of Early Childhood Education) previously seeded at 3 credits; the official graduation map (poid=1526) prints NO credit value (blank Credits cell). Corrected to credits:0 with required_zero:true as the mechanical carrier for the blank (not a genuine zero-credit requirement). PRINTED CONTRADICTION PRESERVED: Semester One prints 'Complete all 15 Hours' but listed non-blank credits total 12; printed program total is 60 but the sequenced sum is 57. Both values documented as printed.",
